From d39beb06e4dad4bd507fd9abd2d9a110b849ac4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chuppatricky <74110004+chuppatricky@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:12:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] frame_gen: space generated frames over the game frame's
 time

The generated frames were presented together with the game frame they lead up
to: with FIFO they took consecutive refreshes and then nothing came until the
next game frame, so the display rate doubled but motion was no smoother. At
1440p 144 Hz with 2x in Ocarina of Time (38-39 game fps, 77 presents a second)
the time between presents ranged 0.35-33 ms (deviation 12.6 ms).

Each frame now carries a present time: the generated ones and the game frame
are spread evenly over the smoothed game frame interval the pacer measures,
and the present thread waits for that time (sleep to 1.5 ms before, then
yield). Frame generation now always uses the present thread, as the render
thread can't wait. Same run: 9.9-19.8 ms between presents (deviation 1.5 ms),
the same game frame rate. EDEN_NX2_FG_PACING=0 presents them at once as before;
EDEN_NX2_PRESENT_TIMING=1 logs the present intervals once a second.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit a7afd16074ca58f0ada88499fbbb1ea5ab26c900)
